  <page_number>175</page_number>
  <running_head>PRO VETERI MEDICINA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>urget,</catchword>
    <signature>H 4</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">oto, perveniat, quid ni venæ pulsant?</l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Docet enim in corde ac arteriis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>ἀλλαχῶ fola prætereuntium succorum copia &amp;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>bullitione celebrari. Non solùm igitur</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>descendens cava, Triumviratu facta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>turgidaque distendi deberet &amp; pulsare;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>sed eò magis succussione arterias supe-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>rare, quò uniuscujusque virtus, si nullâ a-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>dditione vires acquirat eundo, circà</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>cortum, ἰχνεγτέρη vegetior, &amp; infra-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>ior existit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Tantùm abest omnem effervescen-</l>
    <l n="13">tiam esse igneam ut præter evidentis-s-</l>
    <l n="14">imam rationem manifestissimo expe-</l>
    <l n="15">rimento, beneficio Thermometræ;</l>
    <l n="16">e quo suprà, constet dari efferve-</l>
    <l n="17">scentiam non calidam modò sed &amp;</l>
    <l n="18">frigidam, &amp; blandam probetur. Quod <i>ψῦχρον</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>ψεῦδος,</i> quantas illis peperit so-</l>
    <l n="20">licitudines, quantos labores! Sed</l>
    <l n="21">quidnam illud est? <i>Dum, inquit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>aqueum ex ejus, putà Sylvii, placito,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>flumen venas percurrit &amp;c. Si statuat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Sylvii sententiam esse, quod ubique</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>urget,</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes />
</page>
